{
     "type": "text",
     "text": "</exemplars>",
     "cache_control": { "type": "ephemeral" }
   }
   ```
3. **Dynamic User Payload**: The volatile user input, dynamic telemetry variables, and execution timestamps must always be appended *after* the cached boundary.

By guaranteeing that the prefix byte-stream remains 100% byte-for-byte identical across calls, the enterprise achieves sub-millisecond Time-to-First-Token (TTFT) cache reads while slashing input API expenses by 85% to 90%, making dense Few-Shot CoT dramatically more economical than naive un-cached zero-shot prompting.

